Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?Phase=203=20NH15=20diag:=20mode=5Fepcs=5Fpr?=
 =?UTF-8?q?obe=20Phase=20E=20=E2=80=94=20one-byte-per-op?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds Phase E to mode_epcs_probe that reads 4 bytes via ONE
CTRL=FAST_READ per byte read, with addr incremented per byte and
NH10 auto-terminate between ops (CTRL=0 → wait busy=0).  Companion
to wrapper NH15 latch-lock (preceding commit).

Sequence per byte:
  DC_RESET pulse + delay (clear flag, reset cntr)
  *DP_ADDR = base + i
  *DP_CTRL = DC_FAST_READ
  wait flag_data_valid=1
  byte = *DP_DATAOUT
  *DP_CTRL = 0  (NH10 auto-terminate)
  wait busy=0

Expected with NH15: bytes deterministic across boots + iterations;
E byte_i at addr 0..3 should match the first 4 bytes of the factory
ALINX bitstream at flash offset 0 (which itself can be cross-
verified by reading the .pof or by openFPGALoader -r the first
sector).  Without NH15 (refutation): same Phase-C-style race.

Phase A/B/C/D are preserved unchanged for empirical baseline diff —
the C5 RADDR=0x81E85 streaming-counter datum and the D iterations'
post-addr RADDR=0 datum stay valid as historical reference points.

Stage2 ELF size: 17728 → 18024 B (+296 B).
---
 sw/stage2_loader/main.c | 81 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 81 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sw/stage2_loader/main.c b/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
index 855bb50..6180457 100644
--- a/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
+++ b/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
@@ -738,6 +738,87 @@ static void mode_epcs_probe(void)
         }
     }
 
+    /* =================================================================
+     * Phase E — NH15 one-byte-per-op (latch-lock falsification)
+     *
+     * Hypothesis (NH15): the Phase C/D non-deterministic bytes are caused
+     * by the wrapper's latched_dataout being overwritten by every
+     * am_data_valid pulse during a FAST_READ's continuous stream.  Wrapper
+     * NH15 gates the load with !flag_data_valid, so the slot becomes a
+     * 1-deep FIFO: first byte captured, subsequent stream-overflow bytes
+     * dropped.  Firmware here does ONE CTRL=FAST_READ per byte, reading
+     * exactly the first byte at each address.
+     *
+     * Sequence per byte (auto-terminate via NH10, no RDEN_DROP):
+     *   1. DC_RESET pulse + delay (clear flag, reset cntr to known state)
+     *   2. *DP_ADDR = base + i
+     *   3. *DP_CTRL = DC_FAST_READ
+     *   4. wait flag_data_valid=1 (= STATUS.b1)
+     *   5. byte = *DP_DATAOUT (read clears flag)
+     *   6. *DP_CTRL = 0    (NH10 auto-terminate)
+     *   7. wait busy=0
+     *
+     * Expected behavior with NH15:
+     *   - Bytes deterministic across boots + across iterations
+     *   - E byte_i at addr 0..3 should match the first 4 bytes of the
+     *     factory ALINX bitstream at flash offset 0
+     *   - Without NH15 (refutation case): bytes would still race because
+     *     the megafunction streams during firmware's MMIO setup overhead
+     *     for steps 4-6
+     * ================================================================= */
+    uart_puts("[P] --- Phase E: NH15 one-byte-per-op @0 ---\r\n");
+
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < 4u; i++) {
+        uint32_t a = i;
+
+        /* Step 1: reset + delay (NH13 stretcher = 16 sysclk; 32 sw_iters
+         * is comfortably more than that). */
+        *DP_CTRL = DC_RESET;
+        for (volatile int d = 0; d < 32; d++) { /* stretcher delay */ }
+
+        /* Step 2: addr */
+        *DP_ADDR = a;
+
+        /* Step 3: start FAST_READ */
+        *DP_CTRL = DC_FAST_READ;
+
+        /* Step 4: wait DV */
+        uint32_t s = 0;
+        uint32_t wi;
+        for (wi = 0; wi < 1000000u; wi++) {
+            s = *DP_STATUS;
+            if (s & 0x2u) break;
+        }
+
+        uart_puts("[P] E addr=");
+        uart_puthex32(a);
+        uart_puts(" wait_dv wi=");
+        uart_puthex32(wi);
+        uart_puts(" STATUS=");
+        uart_puthex32(s);
+
+        if (s & 0x2u) {
+            /* Step 5: read DATAOUT (clears flag) */
+            uint32_t b = *DP_DATAOUT;
+            uart_puts(" DATAOUT=");
+            uart_puthex32(b);
+            uart_puts("\r\n");
+        } else {
+            uart_puts(" TIMEOUT\r\n");
+            /* Don't break — still need to clear CTRL so megafunction
+             * releases for next iteration. */
+        }
+
+        /* Step 6: clear CTRL (NH10 auto-terminate) */
+        *DP_CTRL = 0;
+
+        /* Step 7: wait busy=0 */
+        for (wi = 0; wi < 10000u; wi++) {
+            if (!(*DP_STATUS & 0x1u)) break;
+        }
+        /* Don't print release wait — keep trace compact. */
+    }
+
     uart_puts("[P] diagnostic DONE\r\n");
 
     #undef DP_BASE
